+  {"lesson":5,"field":"content_html","find":"Romans used both burial and cremation, with cremation becoming fashionable among the elite during the Imperial period before inhumation (burial) returned to favour in the 2nd and 3rd centuries AD, partly under the influence of Eastern religions and later Christianity.","replace":"Romans used both burial and cremation. Cremation was common from the later Republic into the early Empire, then inhumation gradually became more common. The reasons for this change are uncertain.","severity":"MEDIUM","note":"F14: corrects the chronology and removes an unsupported causal claim."},
