.","verdict":"FIX"},{"id":"F16","lesson":3,"field":"content_html","severity":"MEDIUM","claim":"Her often ambiguous or cryptic utterances were then transmitted by the priests in verse.","truth":"Either frame this as one ancient tradition, or remove it: ancient accounts conflict, and whether priests interpreted or versified the Pythia’s words is disputed.","evidence":"Pythia (fetched), Oracle procedure: the role of the prophetai is unclear and proposed interpretations are contested.","verdict":"ADJUDICATE"},{"id":"F17","lesson":4,"field":"content_html","severity":"MEDIUM","claim":"the Parthenon frieze ... depicts the Panathenaic procession","truth":"Retain the conventional identification but label it an interpretation, or teach the rival Erechtheus interpretation; neither should be presented as settled fact.","evidence":"Parthenon (fetched), Function: Connelly’s alternative reading is supported by some scholars and disputed by others.","verdict":"ADJUDICATE"},{"id":"F18","lesson":5,"field":"content_html","severity":"MEDIUM","claim":"placing a coin in the mouth or on the eyes of the deceased ... confirms the literary accounts","truth":"A coin custom is attested but was not universal; evidence supports placement in or on the mouth, not the eyes. Correcting the linked conclusion, flashcard, glossary and checks would require a coordinated rewrite.","evidence":"Charon’s obol (fetched): practice was neither pervasive nor restricted to a coin in the mouth; notes reject a classical coin-on-eye custom. Roman funerary practices (fetched) says it was not consistent everywhere.","verdict":"ADJUDICATE"},{"id":"F19","lesson":5,"field":"content_html","severity":"MEDIUM","claim":"The Genesia was an Athenian public festival" ,"truth":"The lesson also calls Genesia ‘primarily a family affair’ in its practice answer. Resolve the public-versus-familial character from a scholarly source, then make the field, glossary and answer key consistent.","evidence":"Raw L05 contains both claims; OCR specification lists Genesia but does not define its public or private character. The fetched Genesia page provided no substantive article.","verdict":"ADJUDICATE"}],"lessons_clean":[],"summary":"Five lessons checked against the OCR specification and fetched sources. Fifteen surgical factual corrections are supplied; four source-interpretation or multi-field issues require adjudication rather than edits."}

